    {
      "id": 53,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        1840,
        600
      ],
      "size": [
        750,
        1320
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 7,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MiniMax-H3 music video (H3-03, supplied audio)\nTurns a supplied music track into a 3-shot music video. Each shot is a Ref2VA request that uses the shared character/style image and its own slice of the track as driving audio (`audio_mode=lock_source`), so the visuals follow that part of the music. Concatenate Video joins the shots and replaces their audio with the original track.\n\n**Server:** a Ref2VA-capable H3 service (combined, or `--task-type ref2va`). Requires ComfyUI v0.36.0+ for Concatenate Video.\n\n**Inputs:** select your track in *Supplied music track* (WAV/MP3) and your subject in *Character / style reference*. Write one prompt per shot; name the subject `<Picture 1>`.\n\n**Synchronization:** every shot is 124 frames = 124/24 s. Shot *i* (from 0) starts at `track start + i x 5.1667` s, so the slice starts are 0, 5.17 and 10.33 s and the final soundtrack is 3 x 5.1667 = 15.5 s. Keep these in step if you change the shot length, the shot count, or the track start.\n\n**Audio:** *replace* (default) puts the original recording on the final MP4. Disconnect `complete_audio` to keep each shot's returned audio instead: H3's reconstruction of the same slice, which can differ slightly at shot boundaries. `lock_source` keeps the driving audio fixed, so H3 does not add new sound on top of it.\n\n**More shots:** duplicate a shot group, move its slice start by 5.1667 s, connect it to the next free Concatenate Video input, and lengthen the full-track trim.\n\nSee `docs/h3-03-music-video.md`."
      ],
      "title": "How to use this graph"
    }
